# ---- Build artifacts ----
# Anchored to repo root so `cmd/skygate/` (the source dir) is NOT ignored.
# Without the leading slash, `skygate` would match any path segment named
# `skygate` — including the source tree.
/skygate
/skygate.new
/skygate-*-linux-*
*.exe

# ---- Backups & patches ----
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.tar
*.tar.*
*.tgz

# ---- Local-only state ----
.env
/data/
/static/
skygate.db
*.log
*.pid

# ---- Dump/experimental scripts ----
.sg_*.ps1
# One-off investigation / verify / debug / cleanup scripts
# (created during live ops, never intended to be committed).
# They live in the working tree so `ls` and `grep` find them,
# but `git add -A` and `git status` ignore them. If a script
# graduates to "kept" status (used by smoke / docs / release
# tooling), move it to scripts/ or deploy/ and re-add to
# git explicitly.
#
# NOTE: scripts/verify_*.sh are the v0.28.5 guarantee catalog
# (B1-B94 + R1-R35) and ARE committed — they're referenced by
# `make verify-pre` / `make verify-post` in the Makefile. The
# ignore patterns below deliberately only cover the ROOT-level
# verify_* / check_* / etc. (created during debugging), not the
# production ones under scripts/.
check_*.sh
test_*.sh
copy_*.sh
debug_*.sh
/debug.sh
debug.sh

# ---- One-shot investigation scripts (B243 live-debug + reconcile investigation) ----
# Any file matching __* in the root is a one-off probe / debug /
# install / verify script that was created during live ops.
# `__` prefix is the convention; scripts/verify_*.sh + scripts/
# check_b_*.sh are the production ones (committed, referenced by
# Makefile / verify_pre_deploy.sh).
__*.sh
__*.txt
__*.py
__*.md

# Python __pycache__ from scripts/__*.py (the probe scripts above)
__pycache__/

# PowerShell artifact: stray "=NNN" files (0 bytes) that get created
# when a redirect token is mistyped (e.g. `> =140`). Harmless; just
# noise in `git status`.
=*

# Pre-B243 rollback insurance (preserved on the VM at
# /home/skyadmin/skygate/internal/headscale/reconcile.go.b243-pre,
# then deleted after live verified). When the fix ships to git
# the .pre file should be removed.
*.b243-pre
reset_*.sh
fix_*.sh
cleanup_*.sh
deploy_*.sh
run_*.sh
wait_*.sh
check_*.py
check_*.ps1
verify_*.py
verify_*.ps1
test_*.py
test_*.ps1
# Anything explicitly named "test_*" or "check_*" lives under
# scripts/ in the repo (e.g. scripts/check_b91.sh,
# scripts/test_check_https.py); root-level test_*.py / check_*.sh
# is debugging scratch. The "scripts/check_*" and "scripts/test_*"
# allowance is via the explicit `!` override below.
!scripts/check_*.sh
!scripts/test_*.sh

# B- and verify- scripts may generate a tiny .bat to call powershell
# (see scripts/find_go.sh). Gitignored because it's a build artifact.
scripts/_find_go.bat
sg_*.ps1
sg_*.sh
/sg_*.html
/sg_*.txt

# ---- v0.34.0 — additional debug/throwaway patterns ----
# Root-level .bat files (operator's PowerShell release scripts
# left over from deploys). Production deploy lives in deploy/.
# Anchored to root with leading /.
/*.bat
scripts/_find_go.bat
# Root-level version-specific deploy scripts (deploy_v0.33.1.42.sh,
# deploy_v33139_v2.sh, etc.). Canonical: deploy/deploy.sh.
# (deploy_*.sh is already in the patterns above; this is for the
# operator's `<vX.Y.Z>.sh` version-specific copies.)
deploy_*-v*.sh
deploy_*-v*.*.sh
# Operator ad-hoc investigation scripts (state_check*.sh,
# pull_and_verify*.sh, final_verify*.sh, r*_focused_*.sh).
state_check*.sh
pull_*.sh
final_*.sh
r*_focused_*.sh
local_*.sh
vm_*.sh
db_*.sh
full_*.sh
healthz_*.sh
i18n_*.sh
tpl_*.sh
find_*.sh
!scripts/find_go.sh
desc_*.sh
diff_check.sh
do_*.sh
b91_*.sh
backfill_*.sh
build_check*.sh
create_release*.*
# e2e_*.sh: pilot scripts. If one graduates to a regression test
# (referenced in docs / used by smoke), move it to scripts/ and
# re-add to git explicitly.
e2e_*.sh
encrypt_*.sh
# Operator ad-hoc verify scripts at root.
# Production: scripts/verify_*.sh.
verify_*.sh
verify_*.bat
# Backup directories from the B91 / v0.33.1.39 deploy work.
.backup_*/
# Netscape cookie file left by `curl -c` during debug sessions.
# Literal $CK_FILE — no var expansion in gitignore patterns.
$CK_FILE
# Curl cookie jars and other transient debugging state.
*.cookie
*.cookies

# ---- Editor / OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---- Backup output directory ----
backup/

# Hermes agent backup directories (do not commit)
.hermes-*/

# Tailscale authkey (read at runtime by entrypoint.sh if TS_AUTHKEY_FILE=...)
# Created by `docker secret create` during local bring-up; never commit.
secrets/
/secrets/

# v0.27.0: go-sqlite3 fallback когда SKYGATE_DB=postgres:// —
# binary без pq driver создаёт фейковую SQLite с этим именем.
# Если увидишь postgres:/ в git status — обнови бинарник (Phase 1.1)
postgres:/
.trash/
/tmp/

# 2026-09-15: operator debug artifacts dropped to /tmp during live ops.
# These are intentionally NOT in scripts/ — they're one-off diagnostics
# the operator runs from a Make target or power-shell paste. Ignored at
# the repo root so `git status` stays clean between operators.
# /tmp/ (above) only ignores DIRS, not loose files; the patterns below
# catch the loose ones when they end up at the repo root.
/tmp/*.sh
/tmp/*.html
/tmp/*.json
/tmp/*.log
/tmp/*.go
/tmp/*.txt
/tmp/*.py
# Same patterns at the repo root for the case where /tmp symlinks or
# bash injection drops the file in cwd.
*.swp.bak
=*

# ---- Operator's one-off debug / investigation artifacts (2026-09-17) ----
# `check_*.sh`, `debug_*.sh`, `test_*.sh`, `find_*.sh`, `fix_*.sh`
# at the repo root are one-off live-ops investigation scripts.
# Production versions live in scripts/ (scripts/check_b*.sh, scripts/
# verify_*.sh). The allow-list below keeps the production ones
# tracked via the existing `!scripts/check_*.sh` override.
check_*.sh
debug_*.sh
test_*.sh
test_*.go.txt
diag_*.sh
tmp_force*.sh
tmp_rollback.sh
scratch/
scratch_archive/
.scratch_archive/
# /tmp/ is already in .gitignore above; this catches the *files*
# dropped at the repo root by accident (e.g. from a bash paste).

# ---- 2026-09-18: re-assert the production script allow-list ----
# The root-level scratch patterns above (check_*.sh, verify_*.sh, debug_*.sh,
# test_*.sh, ...) are NOT anchored, so they match at any depth and silently
# overrode the `!scripts/check_*.sh` negation earlier in this file —
# gitignore honours the LAST matching rule. The practical effect was that a
# new scripts/check_*.sh could not be committed without `git add -f`, and 15
# files under scripts/ (including verify_b199.sh .. verify_b202.sh) were
# already sitting untracked on the operator's machine while
# verify_pre_deploy.sh referenced them.
#
# These negations come last on purpose. The root-level scratch patterns keep
# working because nothing under scripts/ should be scratch: the convention is
# that production checks live in scripts/ and one-off probes do not.
!scripts/check_*.sh
!scripts/verify_*.sh
# 2026-09-19 RR-12: scripts/lib/db_credentials.sh is the runtime DB-credential
# resolver; the broad 'db_*.sh' pattern above must not swallow it.
!scripts/lib/db_credentials.sh
